(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m5"] = E["hr-m5"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-5-4"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-5-4-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-4","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Development plans","tr":"Gelişim planları","fa":"برنامه‌ی توسعه‌ی فردی"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can recommend training and write a short development plan and request.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda eğitim önerebilecek, kısa bir gelişim planı ve talep yazabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی دوره‌ی آموزشی پیشنهاد بدهی و یک برنامه‌ی توسعه‌ی فردی و درخواست کوتاه بنویسی."},"hook":{"en":"Start a training request with the manager's problem. Managers approve training that solves a problem, not a wish. Omar says yes to numbers, not wishes. Leyla needs verbs that sound like a plan.","tr":"Eğitim talebine yöneticinin sorunuyla başla. Yöneticiler bir isteği değil, bir sorunu çözen eğitimi onaylar. Omar dileklere değil, rakamlara evet der. Leyla'nın talebi plan gibi duran fiillere ihtiyaç duyuyor: recommend attending, would like to train.","fa":"درخواست آموزش را با مشکل مدیر شروع کن. مدیرها آموزشی را تأیید می‌کنند که مشکلی را حل کند، نه اینکه فقط آرزوی کسی را برآورده کند. عمر به عدد «بله» می‌گوید، نه به آرزو. درخواست لیلا به فعل‌هایی نیاز دارد که شبیه برنامه باشند: recommend attending و ⁨would like to train⁩."},"before":{"en":"Write a short training request to a busy manager: their problem first, then the course, the cost and one clear request.","tr":"Meşgul bir yöneticiye kısa bir eğitim talebi yaz: önce onun sorunu, sonra kurs, maliyet ve tek bir net rica.","fa":"برای یک مدیر پرمشغله یک درخواست آموزشی کوتاه بنویس: اول مشکل او، بعد دوره، هزینه و یک درخواست روشن."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Start with their problem, not your wish","tr":"İsteğinle değil, onun sorunuyla başla","fa":"با مشکل مدیر شروع کن، نه خواسته‌ی خودت"},"body":{"en":"\"She would like a course\" gives a busy manager no reason to say yes. So name the problem first, then the training, the cost and who covers the work. End with one clear request.","tr":"\"Bir kursa gitmek istiyor\" yoğun bir yöneticiye evet demesi için neden vermez. Bu yüzden önce sorunu, sonra eğitimi, maliyeti ve işi kimin üstleneceğini söyle. Tek net bir ricayla bitir.","fa":"«دلش می‌خواهد به یک دوره برود» دلیلی برای بله گفتن به مدیر پرمشغله نمی‌دهد. پس اول مشکل را بگو، بعد آموزش، هزینه و اینکه چه کسی کارش را انجام می‌دهد. آخرش هم یک درخواست روشن بگذار."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Recommend attending, would like to develop: -ing or to?","tr":"Recommend attending, would like to develop: -ing mi to mu?","fa":"⁨recommend attending⁩ و ⁨would like to develop⁩: ⁨-ing⁩ یا ⁨to⁩؟"},"steps":[{"en":"These verbs take -ing: recommend, suggest, consider, avoid.","tr":"Bu fiillerden sonra -ing gelir: recommend, suggest, consider, avoid.","fa":"بعد از این فعل‌ها ⁨-ing⁩ می‌آید: ⁨recommend⁩، ⁨suggest⁩، ⁨consider⁩، ⁨avoid⁩.","ex":"I recommend attending the coaching course."},{"en":"These take to + verb: would like, want, plan, hope, need.","tr":"Bunlardan sonra to + fiil gelir: would like, want, plan, hope, need.","fa":"بعد از این‌ها to و فعل می‌آید: would like، want، plan، hope، need.","ex":"Deniz would like to train new drivers."},{"en":"Describe the course with that or which.","tr":"Kursu that ya da which ile tanımla.","fa":"دوره را با that یا which توصیف کن.","ex":"a two-day course that teaches coaching skills"}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Verb","Next verb","Example"],"tr":["Fiil","Sonraki fiil","Örnek"],"fa":["فعل","فعل بعدی","مثال"]},"rows":[["recommend / suggest / consider","-ing","I recommend attending the course."],["would like / want / plan / hope","to + verb","He would like to train new drivers."],["describe the course","that / which + clause","a course that teaches coaching skills"]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish 'katılmasını öneririm' and Persian 'pishnahad mikonam sherkat konad' give no clue about -ing or to, so learners guess. English decides by the first verb; learn them in pairs.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'katılmasını öneririm' yapısı -ing mi to mu olacağına dair ipucu vermez. İngilizcede bunu ilk fiil belirler; fiilleri eşleriyle birlikte öğren.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «پیشنهاد می‌کنم در دوره شرکت کند» و هیچ نشانه‌ای از ⁨-ing⁩ یا ⁨to⁩ نیست. در انگلیسی فعل اول تعیین می‌کند؛ فعل‌ها را جفت‌جفت یاد بگیر."},"wrong":"I recommend to attend the Excel course.","right":"I recommend attending the Excel course."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"At the moment, ... (the problem)","meaning":{"en":"Starts from the manager's problem.","tr":"Yöneticinin sorunundan başlar.","fa":"از مشکلِ خود مدیر شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"I recommend -ing...","meaning":{"en":"Gives the solution.","tr":"Çözümü verir.","fa":"راه‌حل را پیشنهاد می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"The cost is..., and ... can cover...","meaning":{"en":"Answers the two questions every manager asks.","tr":"Her yöneticinin sorduğu iki soruyu cevaplar.","fa":"به دو سؤالی که هر مدیری می‌پرسد جواب می‌دهد."}},{"phrase":"mentor","meaning":{"en":"An experienced person who advises a less experienced one.","tr":"mentor, rehber.","fa":"منتور؛ راهنمای باتجربه"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Training agreements","tr":"Eğitim taahhütnameleri","fa":"تعهدنامه‌ی دوره‌ی آموزشی"},"body":{"en":"Some employers, in the UK and in the Persian Gulf for example, ask staff to sign a training agreement: if you leave within a set time after an expensive course, you may have to repay part of the fee. Rules on what is allowed differ by country, so check the local law and tell the employee clearly before they agree.","tr":"Bazı işverenler, örneğin Birleşik Krallık'ta ve Basra Körfezi'nde, çalışanlardan bir eğitim sözleşmesi imzalamalarını ister: pahalı bir kurstan sonra belirli bir süre içinde ayrılırsan ücretin bir kısmını geri ödemen gerekebilir. Neye izin verildiği ülkeden ülkeye değişir; yerel yasayı kontrol et ve çalışan kabul etmeden önce ona açıkça anlat.","fa":"بعضی کارفرماها، مثلاً در بریتانیا و کشورهای حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس، از کارکنان می‌خواهند یک تعهدنامه‌ی آموزشی امضا کنند: اگر بعد از یک دوره‌ی گران‌قیمت، پیش از مدت معینی از شرکت بروند، ممکن است مجبور شوند بخشی از هزینه را برگردانند (چیزی شبیه «تعهد خدمت» در ایران). اینکه چه چیزی مجاز است در هر کشور فرق می‌کند؛ پس قانون محلی را بررسی کن و پیش از اینکه کارمند موافقت کند، شرایط را روشن به او بگو."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از خواسته تا مشکل و برنامه"},"text":"Facts: Two reports had errors last month. A two-day Excel course costs 900 dirhams. You need a yes by Friday.","item":"Could she go on a course? She would like it.","why":{"en":"Weak: a wish, with no reason. Strong: problem, plan, cost, request.","tr":"Zayıf: nedensiz bir istek. Güçlü: sorun, plan, maliyet, rica.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول یک خواسته است، بدون دلیل. نسخه‌ی دوم مشکل، برنامه، هزینه و درخواست را می‌گوید."},"answer":"Two reports had errors last month. I recommend a two-day Excel course. It costs 900 dirhams. Could you approve it by Friday?","cut":["She would like it."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap what gives a busy manager no reason to say yes.","tr":"Meşgul bir yöneticiye evet demesi için hiçbir neden vermeyen cümleye dokun.","fa":"روی جمله‌ای بزن که به یک مدیر پرمشغله هیچ دلیلی برای «بله» گفتن نمی‌دهد."}},"quick":{"prompt":"Your company asks staff to sign a training agreement before an expensive course. What must you do?","options":["Check the local law and explain the repayment rule before they agree","Ask them to sign after the course","Keep the rule in the small print"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Check the local law and tell them clearly first: the rules on repaying fees differ by country, and the employee must know before agreeing.","tr":"Yerel yasayı kontrol et ve önce açıkça anlat: Ücret iadesiyle ilgili kurallar ülkeden ülkeye değişir ve çalışan kabul etmeden önce bunu bilmelidir.","fa":"قانون محلی را چک کن و اول به‌روشنی توضیح بده: قانون‌های پس دادن هزینه از کشوری به کشور دیگر فرق دارد و کارمند باید قبل از قبول کردن بداند."},"point":4,"hint2":{"en":"A training agreement can cost the employee money later. What do they need before they sign?","tr":"Eğitim sözleşmesi çalışana ileride paraya mal olabilir. İmzalamadan önce neye ihtiyaçları var?","fa":"قرارداد آموزشی ممکن است بعداً برای کارمند خرج داشته باشد. قبل از امضا به چه چیزی نیاز دارد؟"}},"remember":{"en":"Learn the first verb with its partner: recommend + -ing, would like + to. Say them as one chunk. Result of this lesson: you can write a training request a manager can approve. You also have one.","tr":"İlk fiili eşiyle birlikte öğren: recommend + -ing, would like + to. Tek parça gibi söyle. Bu dersin sonucu: bir yöneticinin onaylayabileceği bir eğitim talebi yazabilirsin ve elinde bir tane olur.","fa":"فعل اول را با همراهش یاد بگیر: recommend با -ing و would like با to. مثل یک تکه با هم بگو. حالا می‌توانی درخواست آموزشی بنویسی که مدیر بتواند تأیید کند. یکی هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Verb + person + to: enable him to, would like you to","tr":"Fiil + kişi + to: enable him to, would like you to","fa":"فعل، شخص و to: enable him to، would like you to"},"steps":[{"en":"Verb + person + to + verb.","tr":"Fiil + kişi + to + fiil.","fa":"الگو این است: فعل، شخص، to و فعل دوم.","ex":"This course will enable him to coach new drivers."},{"en":"would like + person + to, never would like that.","tr":"would like + kişi + to; would like that asla.","fa":"بعد از would like اول شخص می‌آید و بعد to؛ هرگز would like that.","ex":"Omar would like Deniz to start in November."},{"en":"Formal extra: It would be worth + -ing.","tr":"Resmî bir ek: It would be worth + -ing.","fa":"یک الگوی رسمی: بعد از It would be worth فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"It would be worth pairing him with Hasan first."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["enable / allow + person + to","The course will enable him to coach new drivers."],["would like / want + person + to","Omar would like Deniz to start in November."],["encourage + person + to","We encourage drivers to share ideas."],["It would be worth + -ing","It would be worth pairing him with Hasan first."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: in your request, use one verb + person + to (enable him to, would like him to) and one \"It would be worth + -ing\".","tr":"B2 yolu: talebinde bir fiil + kişi + to (enable him to, would like him to) ve bir \"It would be worth + -ing\" kullan.","fa":"مسیر B2: در درخواستت یک بار الگوی فعل، شخص و to (مثل enable him to یا would like him to) و یک بار It would be worth با فعل -ing‌دار به کار ببر."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-5-4-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-4","title":"Recommend attending, would like to develop: -ing or to?","titleTr":"Recommend attending, would like to develop: -ing mi to mu?","exp":{"en":"Development plans are full of verbs followed by another verb, and each first verb decides the form. Recommend, suggest, consider and avoid take -ing: \"I recommend attending the coaching course.\", \"He is considering applying for the trainer role.\" Would like, want, plan, hope and need take to + verb: \"Deniz would like to train new drivers.\", \"We plan to start in November.\" The most common errors are \"recommend to attend\" and \"would like developing\". To describe a course or role, add a relative clause with that or which: \"a two-day course that teaches basic coaching skills\".","tr":"Gelişim planları ardından başka bir fiil gelen fiillerle doludur ve ilk fiil biçimi belirler. Recommend, suggest, consider ve avoid -ing alır: \"I recommend attending the coaching course.\", \"He is considering applying for the trainer role.\" Would like, want, plan, hope ve need to + fiil alır: \"Deniz would like to train new drivers.\", \"We plan to start in November.\" En sık hatalar \"recommend to attend\" ve \"would like developing\" biçimleridir. Bir kursu ya da görevi anlatmak için that veya which ile bir sıfat cümlesi ekle: \"a two-day course that teaches basic coaching skills\".","fa":"برنامه‌های توسعه‌ی فردی پر از فعل‌هایی است که بعدشان فعل دیگری می‌آید، و شکلِ فعل دوم را فعل اول تعیین می‌کند. بعد از ⁨recommend⁩، ⁨suggest⁩، ⁨consider⁩ و ⁨avoid⁩ فعل ⁨-ing⁩ می‌آید: «⁨I recommend attending the coaching course.⁩» و «⁨He is considering applying for the trainer role.⁩» بعد از ⁨would like⁩، ⁨want⁩، ⁨plan⁩، ⁨hope⁩ و ⁨need⁩ فعل با ⁨to⁩ می‌آید: «⁨Deniz would like to train new drivers.⁩» و «⁨We plan to start in November.⁩» رایج‌ترین اشتباه‌ها «⁨recommend to attend⁩» و «⁨would like developing⁩» است. چاره‌ای جز حفظ کردن این دو گروه نیست؛ جدول زیر را چند بار با صدای بلند بخوان. برای توصیف یک دوره یا نقش، یک جمله‌ی موصولی با ⁨that⁩ یا ⁨which⁩ اضافه کن: «⁨a two-day course that teaches basic coaching skills⁩»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Verb","Next verb","Example"],"tr":["Fiil","Sonraki fiil","Örnek"],"fa":["فعل","فعل بعدی","مثال"]},"rows":[["recommend / suggest / consider","-ing","I recommend attending the course."],["would like / want / plan / hope","to + verb","He would like to train new drivers."],["describe the course","that / which + clause","a course that teaches coaching skills"]]},"wrong":"I recommend to attend the coaching course.","right":"I recommend attending the coaching course.","blank":{"sentence":"I recommend ___ the coaching course in November.","word":"attending","distractors":["to attend","attend"]},"wrong2":"He would like developing his coaching skills.","right2":"He would like to develop his coaching skills.","blank2":{"sentence":"Deniz would like ___ new drivers.","word":"to train","distractors":["training","train"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Omar says yes to numbers, not wishes. Leyla needs verbs that sound like a plan.","tr":"Omar dileklere değil, rakamlara evet der. Leyla'nın talebi plan gibi duran fiillere ihtiyaç duyuyor: recommend attending, would like to train.","fa":"عمر به عدد «بله» می‌گوید، نه به آرزو. درخواست لیلا به فعل‌هایی نیاز دارد که شبیه برنامه باشند: recommend attending و ⁨would like to train⁩."},"tryWhy":{"en":"attending: recommend is followed by -ing. 'recommend to attend' is the error we hear most.","tr":"attending: recommend'dan sonra -ing gelir. En sık duyduğumuz hata 'recommend to attend'.","fa":"جواب attending است: بعد از recommend فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید. رایج‌ترین خطا recommend to attend است."},"rule":[{"en":"recommend, suggest, consider, avoid + -ing.","tr":"recommend, suggest, consider, avoid + -ing.","fa":"بعد از recommend، suggest، consider و avoid فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"I recommend attending the coaching course."},{"en":"would like, want, plan, hope, need + to + verb.","tr":"would like, want, plan, hope, need + to + fiil.","fa":"بعد از would like، want، plan، hope و need اول to می‌آید و بعد فعل.","ex":"Deniz would like to train new drivers."},{"en":"Describe the course with that or which.","tr":"Kursu that ya da which ile tanımla.","fa":"دوره را با that یا which توصیف کن.","ex":"a two-day course that teaches coaching skills"}],"test":{"en":"Learn the first verb with its partner: recommend + -ing, would like + to. Say them as one chunk.","tr":"İlk fiili eşiyle birlikte öğren: recommend + -ing, would like + to. Tek parça gibi söyle.","fa":"فعل اول را با همراهش یاد بگیر: recommend با -ing و would like با to. مثل یک تکه با هم بگو."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish 'katılmasını öneririm' and Persian 'pishnahad mikonam sherkat konad' give no clue about -ing or to, so learners guess. English decides by the first verb; learn them in pairs.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'katılmasını öneririm' yapısı -ing mi to mu olacağına dair ipucu vermez. İngilizcede bunu ilk fiil belirler; fiilleri eşleriyle birlikte öğren.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «پیشنهاد می‌کنم در دوره شرکت کند» و هیچ نشانه‌ای از ⁨-ing⁩ یا ⁨to⁩ نیست. در انگلیسی فعل اول تعیین می‌کند؛ فعل‌ها را جفت‌جفت یاد بگیر."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["recommend to attend","recommend to send","suggest to attend","suggest to send","consider to apply","avoid to"],"fix":{"en":"recommend, suggest, consider and avoid take -ing: 'I recommend attending the course.'","tr":"recommend, suggest, consider ve avoid -ing alır: 'I recommend attending the course.'","fa":"⁨recommend⁩، ⁨suggest⁩، ⁨consider⁩ و ⁨avoid⁩ فعل ⁨-ing⁩ می‌گیرند: «⁨I recommend attending the course.⁩»"}},{"find":["would like developing","would like training","want developing","plan starting","hope becoming"],"fix":{"en":"would like, want, plan and hope take to + verb: 'He would like to develop his coaching skills.'","tr":"would like, want, plan ve hope to + fiil alır: 'He would like to develop his coaching skills.'","fa":"بعد از would like، want، plan و hope، اول to و بعد فعل می‌آید: «He would like to develop his coaching skills.»"}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-5-4-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-4","title":"Verb + person + to: enable him to, would like you to","titleTr":"Fiil + kişi + to: enable him to, would like you to","exp":{"en":"Many development verbs need a person before the next verb: verb + object + to-infinitive. \"This course will enable him to coach new drivers.\", \"We encourage drivers to share ideas.\", \"Omar would like Deniz to start in November.\" Farsi uses a that-clause here (ke) and Turkish a clause with -masını, which leads to the error \"Omar would like that Deniz starts\". In English use the object + to: \"would like Deniz to start\". Do not drop the person after enable or allow (\"This will enable to coach\" is wrong). A useful formal extra: \"It would be worth + -ing\": \"It would be worth pairing him with Hasan first.\"","tr":"Birçok gelişim fiili, sonraki fiilden önce bir kişi ister: fiil + nesne + to-infinitive. \"This course will enable him to coach new drivers.\", \"We encourage drivers to share ideas.\", \"Omar would like Deniz to start in November.\" Türkçede burada çoğu zaman bir yan cümle kullanılır (\"Omar, Deniz'in kasımda başlamasını istiyor\"), bu da \"Omar would like that Deniz starts\" hatasına yol açar. İngilizcede nesne + to kullan: \"would like Deniz to start\". Enable veya allow fiilinden sonra kişiyi atma (\"This will enable to coach\" yanlış). Yararlı resmî bir ek: \"It would be worth + -ing\": \"It would be worth pairing him with Hasan first.\"","fa":"خیلی از فعل‌هایی که در برنامه‌های توسعه به کار می‌روند، پیش از فعل دوم یک «شخص» لازم دارند: فعل + مفعول + ⁨to⁩ + فعل. «⁨This course will enable him to coach new drivers.⁩»، «⁨We encourage drivers to share ideas.⁩» و «⁨Omar would like Deniz to start in November.⁩» در فارسی اینجا معمولاً از «که» استفاده می‌کنیم («عمر می‌خواهد که دنیز در نوامبر شروع کند»)، و همین باعث می‌شود فارسی‌زبان‌ها بنویسند «⁨Omar would like that Deniz starts⁩». اما در انگلیسی باید مفعول + ⁨to⁩ بیاید: «⁨would like Deniz to start⁩». بعد از ⁨enable⁩ یا ⁨allow⁩ هم شخص را حذف نکن («⁨This will enable to coach⁩» غلط است). یک الگوی رسمی و کاربردی دیگر: ⁨It would be worth⁩ + ⁨-ing⁩ یعنی «می‌ارزد که...»: «⁨It would be worth pairing him with Hasan first.⁩»"},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["enable / allow + person + to","The course will enable him to coach new drivers."],["would like / want + person + to","Omar would like Deniz to start in November."],["encourage + person + to","We encourage drivers to share ideas."],["It would be worth + -ing","It would be worth pairing him with Hasan first."]]},"wrong":"This course will enable to coach new drivers.","right":"This course will enable him to coach new drivers.","blank":{"sentence":"This course will enable him ___ new drivers.","word":"to coach","distractors":["coaching","coach"]},"wrong2":"Omar would like that Deniz starts in November.","right2":"Omar would like Deniz to start in November.","blank2":{"sentence":"It would be worth ___ him with Hasan first.","word":"pairing","distractors":["to pair","pair"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: in your request, use one verb + person + to (enable him to, would like him to) and one \"It would be worth + -ing\".","tr":"B2 yolu: talebinde bir fiil + kişi + to (enable him to, would like him to) ve bir \"It would be worth + -ing\" kullan.","fa":"مسیر B2: در درخواستت یک بار الگوی فعل، شخص و to (مثل enable him to یا would like him to) و یک بار It would be worth با فعل -ing‌دار به کار ببر."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-5-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"We would like you ___ the new drivers next month.","options":["mentoring","to mentor","mentor"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"to mentor: 'would like' + person + to + verb. 'Mentoring' and 'mentor' don't follow 'would like you'.","tr":"to mentor: 'would like' + kişi + to + fiil. 'Mentoring' ve 'mentor' 'would like you'dan sonra gelmez.","fa":"to mentor درست است: would like و شخص و to و فعل. mentoring و mentor بعد از would like you نمی‌آیند."}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"'This course will enable him to coach new drivers.' One verb, one person, then to: the plan in a line.","tr":"'This course will enable him to coach new drivers.' Bir fiil, bir kişi, sonra to: planın tek satırı.","fa":"«⁨This course will enable him to coach new drivers.⁩» یک فعل، یک شخص، بعد to: کل برنامه در یک خط."},"tryWhy":{"en":"pairing: 'It would be worth' is followed by -ing.","tr":"pairing: 'It would be worth'ten sonra -ing gelir.","fa":"جواب pairing است: بعد از It would be worth فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید."},"rule":[{"en":"Verb + person + to + verb.","tr":"Fiil + kişi + to + fiil.","fa":"الگو این است: فعل، شخص، to و فعل دوم.","ex":"This course will enable him to coach new drivers."},{"en":"would like + person + to, never would like that.","tr":"would like + kişi + to; would like that asla.","fa":"بعد از would like اول شخص می‌آید و بعد to؛ هرگز would like that.","ex":"Omar would like Deniz to start in November."},{"en":"Formal extra: It would be worth + -ing.","tr":"Resmî bir ek: It would be worth + -ing.","fa":"یک الگوی رسمی: بعد از It would be worth فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"It would be worth pairing him with Hasan first."}],"test":{"en":"After enable, allow, encourage or would like: is there a person before to? If not, add one.","tr":"enable, allow, encourage ya da would like'tan sonra: to'dan önce bir kişi var mı? Yoksa ekle.","fa":"بعد از enable، allow، encourage یا would like: پیش از to شخصی آمده؟ اگر نه، اضافه کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian 'mikhad ke Deniz shoru konad' uses a that-clause (ke) and Turkish 'Deniz'in kasımda başlamasını istiyor' a clause with -masını; both lead to 'would like that Deniz starts'. English uses person + to.","tr":"Türkçede 'Omar, Deniz'in kasımda başlamasını istiyor' deriz; bu da 'would like that Deniz starts' hatasına yol açar. İngilizcede kişi + to kullanılır: would like Deniz to start.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «عمر می‌خواهد که دنیز در نوامبر شروع کند» و همین باعث می‌شود بنویسیم «would like that Deniz starts». در انگلیسی اول شخص و بعد to می‌آید: «would like Deniz to start»."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["would like that he","would like that deniz","would like that you","want that he","want that you","enable to","allow to coach"],"fix":{"en":"Use person + to: 'Omar would like Deniz to start', 'enable him to coach'.","tr":"Kişi + to kullan: 'Omar would like Deniz to start', 'enable him to coach'.","fa":"اول شخص و بعد to بیاور: «Omar would like Deniz to start» و «enable him to coach»."}},{"find":["worth to pair","worth to send","worth to try"],"fix":{"en":"It would be worth + -ing: 'It would be worth pairing him with Hasan.'","tr":"It would be worth’dan sonra fiil -ing alır: 'It would be worth pairing him with Hasan.'","fa":"بعد از ⁨It would be worth⁩ فعل با ⁨-ing⁩ می‌آید: «⁨It would be worth pairing him with Hasan.⁩»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-5-4-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-4","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Development and Training","tr":"Gelişim ve Eğitim","fa":"توسعه‌ی فردی و آموزش"},"cards":[{"word":"development plan","sentence":"Every driver has a one-page development plan.","meaning":{"en":"A written plan for how someone will grow at work.","tr":"gelişim planı.","fa":"برنامه‌ی توسعه‌ی فردی (برنامه‌ی مکتوب رشد شغلی یک نفر)"}},{"word":"coaching","sentence":"Good coaching helps new drivers learn faster.","meaning":{"en":"Helping someone improve through practice and feedback.","tr":"koçluk.","fa":"کوچینگ؛ مربیگری (کمک به پیشرفت با تمرین و بازخورد)"}},{"word":"mentor","sentence":"Hasan will be his mentor for the first two trainees.","meaning":{"en":"An experienced person who advises a less experienced one.","tr":"mentor, rehber.","fa":"منتور؛ راهنمای باتجربه"}},{"word":"skill gap","sentence":"The main skill gap is giving feedback.","meaning":{"en":"The difference between the skills you have and the skills you need.","tr":"beceri açığı.","fa":"شکاف مهارتی"}},{"word":"training budget","sentence":"There is money left in this year's training budget.","meaning":{"en":"Money planned for courses and learning.","tr":"eğitim bütçesi.","fa":"بودجه‌ی آموزش"}},{"word":"course fee","sentence":"The course fee is 1,800 dirhams.","meaning":{"en":"The price of a course.","tr":"kurs ücreti.","fa":"هزینه‌ی ثبت‌نام دوره"}},{"word":"business case","sentence":"A request needs a business case, not only a wish.","meaning":{"en":"The reasons why something is good for the company.","tr":"iş gerekçesi.","fa":"توجیه تجاری (دلایلی که نشان می‌دهد کاری به نفع شرکت است)"}},{"word":"approve","sentence":"Omar approved the request on Friday.","gap":"approved","accept":["approved","approve"],"meaning":{"en":"To officially say yes.","tr":"onaylamak.","fa":"تأیید کردن؛ رسماً موافقت کردن"}},{"word":"cover","sentence":"Who will cover his route during the course?","meaning":{"en":"To do someone's work while they are away.","tr":"yerine bakmak.","fa":"در نبودِ کسی کارش را انجام دادن؛ جانشین شدن"}},{"word":"career path","sentence":"Driver, then trainer: that is a clear career path.","meaning":{"en":"The steps of a person's career.","tr":"kariyer yolu.","fa":"مسیر شغلی"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-5-4-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-4","title":{"en":"What Makes It a Yes","tr":"Evet Dedirten Şey","fa":"چه چیزی جواب را به «بله» تبدیل می‌کند؟"},"text":"Two days after the appraisal, an email arrived from Deniz. It was three lines long and he had clearly written it many times.\n\n\"Dear Leyla, there is something I did not say on Friday. I would like to help train the new drivers. Hasan says I explain things well. Thank you, Deniz.\"\n\nLeyla smiled at her screen. Then she stopped smiling, because she knew Omar.\n\nOmar did not say yes to wishes. He said yes to numbers.\n\nShe opened a development plan for Deniz. Goal: to develop basic coaching skills. Action one: attend a two-day course in November that teaches coaching for workplace trainers. Course fee: 1,800 dirhams. Action two: shadow Hasan while he trains the next two new drivers. Action three: lead the training of one new driver alone by February, with Hasan as his mentor.\n\nThen she wrote to Omar. Her first draft began, \"Deniz would really like to grow.\" She deleted it. Omar would stop reading there.\n\nThe second draft began with the problem Omar already had. \"Next quarter we will hire twelve new drivers. At the moment Hasan trains everyone alone, and he loses two of his own routes every week to do it.\"\n\nThen the solution: \"I recommend sending Deniz on a two-day coaching course in November. He would like to train new drivers, and he already answers their questions informally.\"\n\nThen the cost and the cover: \"The course fee is 1,800 dirhams. Karim, who joined us on a day route in June, can cover Route 7 for the two days.\"\n\nOmar replied in eleven minutes. That was fast for Omar.\n\n\"Approved. Why didn't he ask me himself?\"\n\nLeyla thought about the truck, the engine off, the sentence said to the windscreen. \"I'll tell you on Thursday,\" she wrote.","vocab":[{"word":"clearly","en":"In a way that is easy to see.","tr":"açıkça, belli ki","fa":"به‌وضوح"},{"word":"wish","en":"Something you want, often without a plan.","tr":"dilek, istek","fa":"آرزو؛ خواسته‌ای که اغلب برنامه‌ای پشتش نیست"},{"word":"quarter","en":"Three months of a business year.","tr":"çeyrek (üç aylık dönem)","fa":"فصل کاری (سه ماه از سال مالی)"},{"word":"informally","en":"Not as part of an official role.","tr":"gayriresmî olarak","fa":"به‌طور غیررسمی (نه به‌عنوان نقش رسمی)"},{"word":"reply","en":"To answer.","tr":"cevap vermek","fa":"پاسخ دادن"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why did Leyla delete \"Deniz would really like to grow\"?","options":["It had a grammar mistake","Omar says yes to business reasons, not wishes","Deniz asked her to"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct sentence.","options":["I recommend sending Deniz on the course.","I recommend to send Deniz on the course.","I recommend send Deniz on the course."],"correct":0},{"prompt":"What problem did the request start with?","options":["The course fee","Hasan training everyone alone and losing routes","Deniz's late reports"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Why might Deniz not have asked Omar himself?","options":["He did not want the job","Asking his manager for more felt risky","He did not have Omar's email"],"correct":1}],"notice":{"en":"Leyla deletes her first draft to Omar after one line. Why? Watch what her second draft starts with.","tr":"Leyla, Omar'a yazdığı ilk taslağı bir satırdan sonra siliyor. Neden? İkinci taslağın neyle başladığına dikkat et.","fa":"لیلا پیش‌نویس اولش برای عمر را بعد از یک خط پاک می‌کند. چرا؟ دقت کن پیش‌نویس دوم با چه شروع می‌شود."},"bridge":{"en":"'I recommend sending Deniz...' and 'He would like to train...' Next: see which verbs take -ing and which take to.","tr":"'I recommend sending Deniz...' ve 'He would like to train...' Sırada: hangi fiillerin -ing, hangilerinin to aldığını gör.","fa":"«⁨I recommend sending Deniz...⁩» و «⁨He would like to train...⁩» قدم بعد: ببین کدام فعل‌ها ⁨-ing⁩ می‌گیرند و کدام ⁨to⁩."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-5-4","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-4","topic":{"en":"Asking for Training Approval","tr":"Eğitim Onayı İstemek","fa":"درخواست تأیید برای یک دوره‌ی آموزشی"},"warmup":{"en":"What is one skill you would like to develop at work next year? Who would need to say yes?","tr":"Gelecek yıl işte geliştirmek istediğin bir beceri nedir? Kimin evet demesi gerekir?","fa":"چه مهارتی را دوست داری سال آینده در کارت تقویت کنی؟ چه کسی باید با آن موافقت کند؟"},"questions":[{"en":"In 60 seconds, ask Omar to approve the course: start with his problem, not the wish.","tr":"60 saniyede Omar'dan kursu onaylamasını iste: dilekle değil, onun sorunuyla başla.","fa":"در ۶۰ ثانیه از عمر بخواه این دوره را تأیید کند. با مشکلِ او شروع کن، نه با خواسته‌ی دنیز."},{"en":"Give the cost, the dates and who will cover the work.","tr":"Maliyeti, tarihleri ve işin yerine kimin bakacağını söyle.","fa":"هزینه و تاریخ‌ها را بگو و اینکه در این مدت چه کسی کارش را انجام می‌دهد."},{"en":"Omar says: \"It's too expensive.\" Answer with one business reason.","tr":"Omar diyor ki: \"Çok pahalı.\" Bir iş gerekçesiyle cevap ver.","fa":"عمر می‌گوید: «⁨It's too expensive.⁩» با یک دلیلِ تجاری جوابش را بده."}],"followups":[{"en":"Make the request in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"Talebi 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede yap.","fa":"درخواست را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه مطرح کن."},{"en":"Now recommend one course or skill for yourself, and say why.","tr":"Şimdi kendin için bir kurs ya da beceri öner ve nedenini söyle.","fa":"حالا یک دوره یا مهارت برای خودت پیشنهاد بده و بگو چرا."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"At the moment, ... (the problem)","meaning":{"en":"Starts from the manager's problem.","tr":"Yöneticinin sorunundan başlar.","fa":"از مشکلِ خود مدیر شروع می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"I recommend -ing...","meaning":{"en":"Gives the solution.","tr":"Çözümü verir.","fa":"راه‌حل را پیشنهاد می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"The cost is..., and ... can cover...","meaning":{"en":"Answers the two questions every manager asks.","tr":"Her yöneticinin sorduğu iki soruyu cevaplar.","fa":"به دو سؤالی که هر مدیری می‌پرسد جواب می‌دهد."}}],"culture":{"en":"Some employers, in the UK and in the Persian Gulf for example, ask staff to sign a training agreement: if you leave within a set time after an expensive course, you may have to repay part of the fee. Rules on what is allowed differ by country, so check the local law and tell the employee clearly before they agree.","tr":"Bazı işverenler, örneğin Birleşik Krallık'ta ve Basra Körfezi'nde, çalışanlardan bir eğitim sözleşmesi imzalamalarını ister: pahalı bir kurstan sonra belirli bir süre içinde ayrılırsan ücretin bir kısmını geri ödemen gerekebilir. Neye izin verildiği ülkeden ülkeye değişir; yerel yasayı kontrol et ve çalışan kabul etmeden önce ona açıkça anlat.","fa":"بعضی کارفرماها، مثلاً در بریتانیا و کشورهای حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس، از کارکنان می‌خواهند یک تعهدنامه‌ی آموزشی امضا کنند: اگر بعد از یک دوره‌ی گران‌قیمت، پیش از مدت معینی از شرکت بروند، ممکن است مجبور شوند بخشی از هزینه را برگردانند (چیزی شبیه «تعهد خدمت» در ایران). اینکه چه چیزی مجاز است در هر کشور فرق می‌کند؛ پس قانون محلی را بررسی کن و پیش از اینکه کارمند موافقت کند، شرایط را روشن به او بگو."},"model":"Omar, at the moment Hasan trains every new driver alone, and he loses two routes a week. Next quarter we will hire twelve more. I recommend sending Deniz on a two-day coaching course in November. He would like to train new drivers, and he already answers their questions. The course costs 1,800 dirhams, and Karim can cover Route 7 for the two days. Could you approve it by Friday?","selfCheck":[{"en":"I started with Omar's problem, not the wish.","tr":"Dilekle değil, Omar'ın sorunuyla başladım.","fa":"با مشکل عمر شروع کردم، نه با آرزو."},{"en":"I used recommend + -ing and would like + to.","tr":"recommend + -ing ve would like + to kullandım.","fa":"از recommend با -ing و would like با to استفاده کردم."},{"en":"I gave the cost, the dates and the cover.","tr":"Maliyeti, tarihleri ve yerine kimin bakacağını söyledim.","fa":"هزینه، تاریخ‌ها و جانشین را گفتم."},{"en":"I ended with a clear request and a date.","tr":"Net bir talep ve bir tarihle bitirdim.","fa":"با یک درخواست روشن و یک تاریخ تمام کردم."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-5-4-w","title":{"en":"The training request to Omar","tr":"Omar'a eğitim talebi","fa":"درخواست آموزش از عمر"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-4","type":"writing","difficulty":"hard","prompt":{"en":"Write the training request email to Omar (80-110 words): start with his problem, recommend the course, describe it with a that/which clause, give the cost and the cover, and end with a clear request.","tr":"Omar'a eğitim talebi e-postasını yaz (80-110 kelime): onun sorunuyla başla, kursu öner, kursu that/which cümlesiyle anlat, maliyeti ve yerine bakacak kişiyi söyle ve net bir taleple bitir.","fa":"ایمیل درخواست دوره‌ی آموزشی را برای عمر بنویس (۸۰ تا ۱۱۰ کلمه): با مشکل او شروع کن، دوره را پیشنهاد بده، آن را با یک جمله‌ی that یا which توصیف کن، هزینه و جانشین را بگو و با یک درخواست روشن تمام کن."},"model":"Dear Omar, Next quarter we will hire twelve new drivers. At the moment Hasan trains everyone alone, and he loses two of his own routes every week to do it. I recommend sending Deniz on a two-day course in November that teaches basic coaching skills. He would like to train new drivers, and he already answers their questions informally. The course fee is 1,800 dirhams, and Karim can cover Route 7 for the two days. Could you approve this by Friday so that I can book a place? Kind regards, Leyla","frame":"Dear ___, Next quarter we will ___. At the moment ___. I recommend ___ on a ___ course that ___. He would like to ___, and ___. The course fee is ___, and ___ can cover ___. Could you approve this by ___ so that ___? Kind regards, ___","words":[{"word":"recommend"},{"word":"would like to"},{"word":"approve"}],"minWords":80,"minSentences":7,"rubric":["Task done: problem, recommendation, course, cost, cover, request","Organised: problem first, then solution, then practical details","Language: recommend + -ing; would like + to; that/which clause","Tone: business-focused and brief"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: sorun, öneri, kurs, maliyet, yerine bakacak kişi, talep","Düzen: önce sorun, sonra çözüm, sonra pratik ayrıntılar","Dil: recommend + -ing; would like + to; that/which ile yan cümle","Üslup: işe odaklı ve kısa"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: مشکل، پیشنهاد، دوره، هزینه، جانشین در غیابش، درخواست","نظم: اول مشکل، بعد راه‌حل، بعد جزئیات عملی","زبان: recommend با -ing؛ would like با to؛ جمله‌ی موصولی با that/which","لحن: کاری و کوتاه"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"His problem","tr":"Onun sorunu","fa":"مشکل او"},"find":["next quarter","at the moment","loses"],"sample":"twelve new drivers; Hasan trains them all alone"},{"t":{"en":"The course you recommend","tr":"Önerdiğin kurs","fa":"دوره‌ای که پیشنهاد می‌کنی"},"find":["i recommend","course"],"sample":"a two-day coaching course in November"},{"t":{"en":"The cost and the cover","tr":"Maliyet ve yerine bakacak kişi","fa":"هزینه و کسی که جایش کار می‌کند"},"find":["fee","dirhams","cover"],"sample":"1,800 dirhams; Karim covers Route 7"},{"t":{"en":"One clear request","tr":"Tek bir net rica","fa":"یک درخواست روشن"},"find":["could you approve","approve","by friday"],"sample":"approve it by Friday so I can book a place"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-5-4-p","title":{"en":"Omar between two problems","tr":"İki sorun arasında Omar","fa":"عمر میان دو مشکل"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-4","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Omar, reading Leyla's request between two warehouse problems. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: which line made you say yes, and what would have made you say no?","tr":"İki depo sorunu arasında Leyla'nın talebini okuyan Omar'sın. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: hangi satır sana evet dedirtti ve ne olsaydı hayır derdin?","fa":"تو عمر هستی و درخواست لیلا را بین دو گرفتاری انبار می‌خوانی. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: کدام جمله باعث شد «بله» بگویی، و چه چیزی باعث می‌شد «نه» بگویی؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-5-4-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-4","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-5-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"I suggest ___ the course in spring.","options":["to book","booking","book"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"booking: 'suggest' takes -ing. 'To book' and 'book' don't follow suggest this way.","tr":"booking: 'suggest' -ing alır. 'To book' ve 'book' suggest'ten sonra bu şekilde gelmez.","fa":"booking درست است، چون بعد از suggest فعل ing‌دار می‌آید. to book و book این‌طور بعد از suggest نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-5-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"Hana would like ___ more about route planning.","options":["to learn","learning","learn"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"to learn: 'would like' takes to + verb. 'Learning' and 'learn' don't follow would like.","tr":"to learn: 'would like' to + fiil alır. 'Learning' ve 'learn' would like'tan sonra gelmez.","fa":"to learn درست است، چون would like با to و فعل می‌آید. learning و learn بعد از would like نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-5-4","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which opening is most likely to get a busy manager's yes?","options":["Deniz would really like to grow.","Next quarter we will hire twelve drivers, and Hasan trains them all alone.","I have a small favour to ask."],"correct":1,"point":1,"why":{"en":"It starts with the manager's own problem: twelve new drivers and one trainer. 'Deniz would like to grow' and 'a small favour' start from your wish.","tr":"Yöneticinin kendi sorunuyla başlar: on iki yeni şoför ve tek eğitmen. 'Deniz would like to grow' ve 'a small favour' senin isteğinle başlar.","fa":"با مشکل خود مدیر شروع می‌کند: دوازده راننده‌ی جدید و یک آموزش‌دهنده. «Deniz would like to grow» و «a small favour» از خواسته‌ی تو شروع می‌شوند."}},{"from":"hr-5-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"___ the summer was hard, he met every target.","options":["However","Despite","Although"],"correct":2,"point":2,"why":{"en":"Although: a full clause follows (the summer was hard). 'However' starts a new sentence, and 'Despite' needs a noun.","tr":"Although: ardından tam bir yan cümle gelir (the summer was hard). 'However' yeni bir cümle başlatır; 'Despite' isim ister.","fa":"Although درست است، چون بعدش جمله‌ی کامل می‌آید. however جمله‌ی تازه شروع می‌کند و despite اسم می‌خواهد."},"hint2":{"en":"A whole clause follows the gap (the summer was hard). Which word joins a clause, not a noun, and can start the sentence?","tr":"Boşluktan sonra tam bir yan cümle geliyor (the summer was hard). Hangi kelime bir ismi değil, bir yan cümleyi bağlar ve cümleyi başlatabilir?","fa":"بعد از جای خالی یک جمله‌ی کامل آمده (⁨the summer was hard⁩). کدام کلمه یک جمله را وصل می‌کند، نه یک اسم را، و می‌تواند اول جمله بیاید؟"}},{"from":"hr-5-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Leave early ___ avoid the traffic.","options":["to","for","for to"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"to: to + verb gives the purpose. 'For' + verb is wrong for purpose, and 'for to' is not English.","tr":"to: to + fiil amacı verir. Amaç için 'for' + fiil yanlıştır; 'for to' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"to درست است، چون to و فعل هدف را می‌گوید. for با فعل برای هدف غلط است و for to انگلیسی نیست."},"hint2":{"en":"The gap gives a purpose, and a base verb (avoid) follows it. Which option works before a verb?","tr":"Boşluk bir amaç veriyor ve ardından yalın bir fiil (avoid) geliyor. Hangi seçenek bir fiilden önce kullanılır?","fa":"جای خالی هدف را می‌گوید و بعدش یک فعل ساده (⁨avoid⁩) آمده. کدام گزینه قبل از فعل می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-4-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"You are not allowed ___ the trucks home.","options":["take","to take","taking"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"to take: 'be allowed' takes to + verb. 'Take' drops to, and 'taking' doesn't follow allowed this way.","tr":"to take: 'be allowed' to + fiil alır. 'Take' to'yu düşürür; 'taking' allowed'dan sonra bu şekilde gelmez.","fa":"to take درست است، چون be allowed با to و فعل می‌آید. take بدون to است و taking این‌طور بعد از allowed نمی‌آید."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
